   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public officers law, in relation to the qualifications for\nholding the office of assistant district attorney in the county of Orleans",
    "basePrintNo": "S7870",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7870-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Public Officers Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7870\n\nSPONSOR: ORTT\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public officers law, in relation to the qualifica-\ntions for holding the office of  assistant district  attorney  in the\ncounty of Orleans\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 allows Orleans County to hire as assistant district attorneys\nNew York State residents who do not reside in Orleans County.\n\nSection 2 sets forth the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation comes at the request of the Orleans County District\nAttorney. Currently, Orleans County can only hire ADAs from within Orle-\nans County, giving them a limited selection pool. Allowing Orleans Coun-\nty to accept applicants from other counties would help alleviate the\nburden of population loss and ensure that the county is staffed with an\nample amount of qualified ADAs.\n\nCurrently, the Public Officers Law affords this benefit to fourteen\nother upstate counties (Lewis, Cayuga, Madison, Schuyler, Yates, Mont-\ngomery, Putnam, Fulton, Essex, Wyoming, Sullivan, Oswego, Chenango, and\nWashington).\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
